{"id":"zabad","name":"Zabad","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:zabad"],"types":[{"type":"person","from":"UBS: Names of People"}],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Zabad","text":"Gift. (1.) One of David’s valiant men (1 Chr. 11:41), the descendant of Ahlai, of the “children of Sheshan” (2:31). (2.) A descendant of Tahath (7:21). (3.) The son of Shemath. He conspired against Joash, king of Judah, and slew him (2 Chr. 24:25, 26). He is called also Jozachar (2 Kings 12:21). (4.) Ezra 10:27. (5.) Ezra 10:33. (6.) Ezra 10:43."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2066","lemma":"זָבָד","xlit":"Zâbâd","gloss":"Zabad, the name of seven Israelites","kjv":"Zabad","count":8,"share":0.73},{"strong":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","xlit":"yâlad","gloss":"to bear young","kjv":"bear, beget, birth, born","count":3,"share":0.27},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":8,"share":0.73},{"strong":"H1","lemma":"אָב","xlit":"ʼâb","gloss":"father, in a literal and immediate, or figurative and remote application","kjv":"chief, father, patrimony, principal","count":3,"share":0.27}],"verses":["1Chr.2.36","1Chr.2.37","1Chr.7.21","1Chr.11.41","2Chr.24.26","Ezra.10.27","Ezra.10.33","Ezra.10.43","2Kgs.12.21","2Chr.25.3","2Chr.25.4"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"jebusites","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.05,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"amminadab","type":"lexical","strong":"H3205","why":"both lead with יָלַד (H3205)"},{"id":"arphaxad","type":"lexical","strong":"H3205","why":"both lead with יָלַד (H3205)"},{"id":"attai","type":"lexical","strong":"H3205","why":"both lead with יָלַד (H3205)"},{"id":"azariah","type":"lexical","strong":"H3205","why":"both lead with יָלַד (H3205)"},{"id":"barrenness","type":"lexical","strong